.TH FL-WEBCAM 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-webcam \- take photos and record videos with a camera
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-webcam\fR [\fB\-\-software\fR] [\fB\-\-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a live preview of a camera and takes photos or records videos. Cameras are found with
GStreamer's device monitor (Video4Linux and PipeWire cameras); the bar picks the camera and its
resolution. \fBPhoto\fR and \fBVideo\fR switch the shutter button between taking a picture and
starting / stopping a recording; the self-timer waits 3 or 10 seconds first (press the shutter
again to cancel). Space or Enter press the shutter, F or F11 and a double click toggle full screen.
.PP
Photos are saved as JPEG (or PNG, from the menu) in \fI~/Pictures/Webcam\fR, videos as WebM
(VP8 video, Opus sound from the default microphone) in \fI~/Videos/Webcam\fR. The microphone
button turns the sound of recordings on or off. The preview is mirrored by default like a mirror;
the saved photos and videos are not. The button with the thumbnail opens the last photo or video.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-software\fR
Draw the preview without OpenGL (also \fBFLD_VIDEO_SW=1\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-test\fR
Use a moving test pattern instead of a camera (also \fBFLD_WEBCAM_SOURCE=test\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/webcam.ini\fR
[Webcam] Camera, Resolution, Mode (photo or video), Mirror, RecordSound, Timer (0, 3, 10) and
PhotoFormat (jpg or png).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBFLD_WEBCAM_DEBUG\fR
Print GStreamer error details.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-media-player\fR(1), \fBfl-view\fR(1)
